==================================================
6. SAMPLE DATA MUST NOT BE STORED
==================================================

The provider must return an in-memory object.

There must be:

NO:

repository.save(...)
invoiceRepository.save(...)
customerRepository.save(...)
journalRepository.save(...)

and no database mutation whatsoever.

The request lifecycle should be:

HTTP request
    ↓
load template
    ↓
create sample InvoiceDocumentModel
    ↓
apply requested configuration
    ↓
render Thymeleaf
    ↓
return HTML
    ↓
request ends

==================================================
7. APPLY UNSAVED DESIGN CONFIGURATION
==================================================

This is one of the most important requirements.

The sample preview must use the configuration sent by the frontend.

For example:

If frontend sends:

primaryColor = "#2563EB"

the generated HTML must use that color.

If frontend sends:

layout = "MODERN"

the Modern invoice template/layout must be rendered.

If frontend sends:

logoPosition = "CENTER"

the rendered invoice must reflect that.

If frontend sends:

showBillingAddress = false

the billing address must not be displayed.

If frontend sends:

invoiceTitle = "TAX INVOICE"

the generated HTML must display:

TAX INVOICE

The preview must therefore use:

CURRENT UNSAVED DESIGNER CONFIGURATION

rather than only the saved template configuration.

==================================================
8. DO NOT PERSIST THE REQUEST CONFIGURATION
==================================================

The configuration submitted to sample-preview must NOT be saved.

This endpoint is strictly:

READ/RENDER ONLY.

For example:

POST /sample-preview

must NOT update:

DocumentTemplate
DocumentTemplateDesign
DocumentTemplateContent

or any other database entity.

The actual Save operation remains a separate endpoint.

==================================================
9. REUSE EXISTING THYMELEAF RENDERING
==================================================

Do not create a second invoice HTML renderer.

Reuse the existing Thymeleaf rendering service.

If the existing service looks conceptually like:

InvoiceTemplateRenderer

or:

DocumentTemplateRenderer

reuse it.

The target architecture is:

SamplePreviewService
        ↓
InvoiceSampleDataProvider
        ↓
InvoiceDocumentModel
        ↓
Existing DocumentTemplateRenderer
        ↓
Thymeleaf
        ↓
HTML String

If the existing rendering service currently requires an Invoice entity, refactor it carefully so that the lower-level rendering layer accepts the document model instead.

Do not duplicate rendering logic.

==================================================
10. TEMPLATE SELECTION
==================================================

The selected template must determine the layout.

For example:

CLASSIC
MODERN
PROFESSIONAL

If the existing architecture uses template files, resolve the correct Thymeleaf template through the existing template-resolution mechanism.

Do not hardcode HTML strings inside the controller.

The controller must never contain invoice HTML.

==================================================
11. CONTROLLER
==================================================

Create an appropriate controller method.

Conceptually:

@PostMapping("/{templateId}/sample-preview")
public ResponseEntity<String> samplePreview(
        @PathVariable Long templateId,
        @RequestBody SamplePreviewRequest request
)

Use the project's actual ID type and API conventions.

Set:

Content-Type: text/html

Return the rendered HTML.

Do not return:

{
    "html": "..."
}

unless the existing API convention specifically requires that.

The frontend needs the response directly as HTML.

==================================================
12. SERVICE
==================================================

Keep the controller thin.

The controller should delegate to something like:

DocumentTemplatePreviewService

or:

InvoiceTemplatePreviewService

The service should:

1. Retrieve template
2. Validate template ownership/type
3. Build sample document model
4. Apply unsaved design/content configuration
5. Render using existing Thymeleaf renderer
6. Return HTML

==================================================
13. ERROR HANDLING
==================================================

Use the existing application's standard exception handling.

Handle at minimum:

404:
Template not found.

400/422:
Template is not an invoice template.

400/422:
Invalid template configuration.

500:
Unable to render template.

Never expose:

- Java stack traces
- SQL errors
- internal class names
- filesystem paths

to the frontend.

==================================================
14. SECURITY
==================================================

The endpoint must respect the application's existing:

- authentication
- authorization


Do not bypass existing security filters.

==================================================
15. FUTURE EXTENSIBILITY
==================================================

The sample-data architecture must be extensible.

Design it so that later we can add:

InvoiceSampleDataProvider
CreditNoteSampleDataProvider
QuoteSampleDataProvider
PaymentReceiptSampleDataProvider
CustomerStatementSampleDataProvider

without changing the controller architecture.

For example:

DocumentType
    ↓
SampleDataProviderResolver
    ↓
InvoiceSampleDataProvider

For THIS implementation only INVOICE is required.

==================================================
16. TESTS
==================================================

Add appropriate unit/integration tests.

At minimum test:

1. Existing template can generate sample preview.

2. Nonexistent template returns 404.

3. Non-INVOICE template is rejected.

4. Sample preview does not create database records.

5. Unsaved configuration affects generated HTML.

For example:

primaryColor = "#FF0000"

should result in the rendered HTML containing the configured value.

6. Sample data contains realistic invoice information.

7. Template ownership/business isolation is respected.

